<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.rafael0rueda.Tempera</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <name>Tempera</name>
  <summary>Draw and edit raster images</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Tempera is a straightforward raster paint application for the GNOME desktop, in the
      spirit of the classic Paint. It gives you the core drawing tools and gets out of
      the way.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pencil, brush, airbrush and eraser, which can rub back to transparency</li>
      <li>Nine shapes — line, curve, arrow, rectangle, rounded rectangle, ellipse, triangle, star and polygon — filled or outlined, with Shift for squares, circles and 45° lines, and grips to resize or move each one before it lands</li>
      <li>Text in any font installed on the system</li>
      <li>Flood fill with an adjustable tolerance, and a colour picker</li>
      <li>Colours of any opacity, with the ones painted with lately kept beside the palette</li>
      <li>Rectangular and free-form selection to move, copy, cut, stretch or crop to</li>
      <li>Paste screenshots and drop images straight onto the canvas</li>
      <li>Resize the picture, or the canvas around it, and rotate or flip it</li>
      <li>Zoom from 10% to 800% or to fit the window, with crisp pixels and an optional pixel grid when zoomed in; pan with the middle mouse button or pinch on a touchpad</li>
      <li>Undo and redo history, and a list of recently opened files</li>
      <li>Unsaved work is kept safe and offered back after a crash</li>
      <li>Print, fitted to the page or at actual size, with a preview</li>
      <li>A bigger interface, from 100% to 200%, for text, buttons and icons alike</li>
      <li>Keyboard shortcuts you can change to suit you, and every action reachable from the keyboard</li>
      <li>A colour palette beside the canvas, under the tools or along the bottom</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Tempera works entirely offline: it never connects to the network and keeps every
      image on your own machine.
    </p>
  </description>
  <developer id="io.github.rafael0rueda">
    <name>Rafael Rueda</name>
  </developer>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/rafael0rueda/tempera</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/rafael0rueda/tempera/issues</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/rafael0rueda/tempera</url>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.rafael0rueda.Tempera.desktop</launchable>
  <!-- The app was called Hue, under this ID, until it was renamed. -->
  <replaces>
    <id>io.github.rafael0rueda.Hue</id>
  </replaces>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1"/>
  <branding>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="light">#dc8add</color>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="dark">#613583</color>
  </branding>
  <requires>
    <display_length compare="ge">480</display_length>
  </requires>
  <recommends>
    <control>pointing</control>
  </recommends>
  <supports>
    <control>keyboard</control>
  </supports>
  <screenshots>
    <screenshot type="default">
      <caption>Painting a landscape with the brush</caption>
      <image type="source" width="1120" height="800">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rafael0rueda/tempera/v1.3.0/data/screenshots/main-window.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>The dark style, with a selection drawn by hand with Free Select</caption>
      <image type="source" width="1120" height="800">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rafael0rueda/tempera/v1.3.0/data/screenshots/dark-style.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>A filled star waiting with grips to resize it, at a bigger interface size</caption>
      <image type="source" width="1120" height="800">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rafael0rueda/tempera/v1.3.0/data/screenshots/interface-size.png</image>
    </screenshot>
  </screenshots>
  <categories>
    <category>Graphics</category>
    <category>RasterGraphics</category>
  </categories>
  <releases>
    <release version="1.3.0" date="2026-09-25">
      <description>
        <p>A new layout that follows GNOME's design, with less clutter around the picture.</p>
        <p>New features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The options of the tool in hand sit in a bar above the canvas, which names the tool and shows only what applies to it</li>
          <li>Shapes have separate Outline and Fill buttons, so a shape can be all fill, and the nine shapes are one click away in a row</li>
          <li>The primary and secondary colours overlap as two squares, the palette is the twenty GNOME colours, and the paint tools show the primary colour on their icons</li>
          <li>Recent colours are the last six painted with, rather than every colour clicked</li>
          <li>The palette starts on the right, and can still go under the tools or along the bottom</li>
          <li>The header shows the image size, and a status bar has the pointer position, the selection and image sizes and zoom buttons</li>
          <li>The main menu has rows of buttons to rotate, flip and zoom; Shift+Ctrl+R turns the image counterclockwise</li>
          <li>New icons throughout, and the tools are called Color Picker, Rectangle Select and Free Select</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.2.0" date="2026-09-20">
      <description>
        <p>Shapes can now be put right before they land.</p>
        <p>New features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A shape waits after it is drawn, with grips to resize it: a dashed box with a grip on every corner and side for the rectangle, rounded rectangle, ellipse, triangle and star, and grips on their own ends, bends and corners for the line, arrow, curve and polygon</li>
          <li>Shift on a grip squares a shape up or snaps a point to 45°, dragging inside slides the whole shape, and the arrow keys nudge it a pixel at a time</li>
          <li>The colour, size and Fill shape apply to a shape while it waits, so it can be restyled before it lands</li>
          <li>Enter lands the shape and Esc drops it; drawing somewhere else lands the one waiting and starts the next. However it lands, it is a single step to undo</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Fixes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The colour picker keeps the colour it picked, instead of turning the swatch black</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.1.0" date="2026-09-19">
      <description>
        <p>Tempera 1.1 brings more ways to draw and select, printing, and a bigger interface for those who need it.</p>
        <p>New features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The Shapes tool gathers nine shapes in one place: line, curve, arrow, rectangle, rounded rectangle, ellipse, triangle, star and polygon</li>
          <li>The airbrush sprays paint that builds up while the button is held, with an adjustable density</li>
          <li>The lasso selects any shape drawn by hand, to move, copy, cut, delete or crop to</li>
          <li>Show Pixel Grid (Ctrl+G) draws a line between pixels from 400% zoom</li>
          <li>Print (Ctrl+P), fitted to the page or at actual size, with a preview first</li>
          <li>Unsaved work is copied every 30 seconds and offered back after a crash</li>
          <li>Preferences (Ctrl+,) can make text, buttons and icons bigger, up to 200%</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Improvements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Fill shape shows the colour a shape will be filled with</li>
          <li>The selection outline stays one screen pixel thin at every zoom</li>
          <li>The handles of a small selection no longer get in the way of moving it</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.0" date="2026-09-17">
      <description>
        <p>Tempera 1.0 rounds out the essentials of a paint program.</p>
        <p>New features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Resize Image (Ctrl+R) stretches or shrinks the picture itself, in pixels or as a percentage</li>
          <li>Zoom to Fit (Ctrl+9), and an image larger than the window opens fitted to it</li>
          <li>Drag with the middle mouse button to move around the image, or pinch on a touchpad to zoom</li>
          <li>Colours can be see-through, and the ones picked lately gather beside the palette</li>
          <li>Each tool shows its own options: filled shapes, erasing to transparency, fill tolerance and the font</li>
          <li>A new image can start transparent</li>
          <li>The window size, tool, sizes, font, colours and JPEG quality are remembered</li>
          <li>[ and ] make the brush smaller or bigger, and the bottom bar shows the size of a selection</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Improvements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Undo keeps only the part of the image an edit changed, so large photos keep their full history using far less memory</li>
          <li>The sidebar keeps the same width whichever tool is in hand</li>
          <li>Enlarging an image no longer leaves its right and bottom edges faded</li>
          <li>Every release comes with a Flatpak bundle to download from GitHub</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.5.0" date="2026-09-17">
      <description>
        <p>Fixes and improvements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Photos open the right way up, following the orientation the camera recorded</li>
          <li>Reading and writing happen in the background, so a large image no longer freezes the window</li>
          <li>Saving never writes one format's data under another format's name, and an image opened from a format Tempera cannot write, such as GIF, is never overwritten</li>
          <li>Only Save As asks for a JPEG quality; Ctrl+S keeps the one chosen</li>
          <li>Ctrl+Q closes every window, asking in each one with unsaved changes</li>
          <li>Cancelling the save prompt leaves a floating paste or typed text exactly as it was</li>
          <li>Text an input method is still composing shows underlined at the caret</li>
          <li>Saving to a network location no longer crashes</li>
          <li>GIF and ICO images can be opened from the file dialog and the file manager</li>
          <li>The About window names the author and links to the project and its release notes</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Privacy and accessibility:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Recent Files follows the desktop's File History setting, and can be cleared from the menu</li>
          <li>Files that are not ordinary images, such as named pipes, are refused instead of hanging the app</li>
          <li>The colour palette can be used with the keyboard, and buttons, swatches and the canvas announce themselves to screen readers</li>
          <li>Every string is ready to be translated, though Tempera still ships in English only</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.4.0" date="2026-09-17">
      <description>
        <p>Hue is now called Tempera, a name it can keep without clashing with other products.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your settings, keyboard shortcuts and recent files are carried over from Hue the first time Tempera starts</li>
          <li>The app ID is now io.github.rafael0rueda.Tempera, and the project lives at github.com/rafael0rueda/tempera</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.3.0" date="2026-09-17">
      <description>
        <p>New features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Change any keyboard shortcut from the new Keyboard Shortcuts window (Ctrl+?)</li>
          <li>Place the colour palette along the bottom, under the tools or right of the canvas</li>
          <li>The image is centred when the window has room around it, such as when maximised</li>
          <li>Scroll over the zoom level in the bottom bar to zoom in or out</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Fixes and improvements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A refreshed look, with the canvas set in a rounded card inside one continuous frame</li>
          <li>The window closes on the first click when there are no unsaved changes</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.2.0" date="2026-09-16">
      <description>
        <p>New features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Zoom with Ctrl+scroll or Ctrl+plus and minus, with crisp pixels when zoomed in</li>
          <li>Rotate, flip and crop the image to a selection</li>
          <li>Stretch a selection or a pasted image with its handles, and nudge it with the arrow keys</li>
          <li>Shift draws squares, circles and 45° lines</li>
          <li>Recent Files, and a quality setting when saving as JPEG</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Fixes and improvements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Saving can no longer destroy the original file if it fails</li>
          <li>Images too large to edit are refused instead of exhausting memory</li>
          <li>Flood fill is many times faster</li>
          <li>Undo history is capped by memory, and undoing back to the saved image clears the unsaved-changes marker</li>
          <li>The Flatpak no longer needs access to the Pictures folder</li>
          <li>Fixed missing toolbar icons in the Flatpak</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.0" date="2026-09-03">
      <description><p>First release with the core drawing tools.</p></description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
